# `dfo::PSBasisFamily`

The set of directions the poll is built on.

`Canonical` uses the coordinate axes at every iteration, so the same points recur after each mesh refinement (the cache then answers them). `RandomOrtho` (the default) draws a random orthonormal basis, refreshed every `basis_refresh_interval` iterations, so the poll can follow a diagonal or curved boundary and never revisits a point. With constraints a coordinate poll cannot move along a diagonal boundary and can stop at a feasible point that is not optimal.

## Fields

### `Canonical`

`enumerator`, default `0`.

The coordinate axes.

### `RandomOrtho`

`enumerator`, default `1`.

A random orthonormal basis, refreshed periodically.

## Guidance

Set as `PSConfig::basis_family`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

A diagonal constraint. The coordinate basis stops short of the optimum `(1, 1)` of `Σ (xᵢ − 3)²` on `x₀ + x₁ ≤ 2`; the random basis finds it.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto f = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };   // minimum 0 at (3, 3)

  for (const auto family : {dfo::PSBasisFamily::Canonical, dfo::PSBasisFamily::RandomOrtho}) {
    dfo::PSConfig config;
    config.basis_family = family;
    config.nonlinear_constraints = [](const Series &x) {
      dfo::PSConstraintValues v;
      v.inequality = (x.sum() - 2.0).reshape({1});
      return v;
    };
    const dfo::PSOutcome o = dfo::pattern_search_minimizer(f, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), config);
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(family), ": minimizer =", o.minimizer.items<double>(), ", minimum =", o.minimum);
  }
}
```

### Example 2

The cache. The coordinate basis revisits points after each mesh refinement; the random basis does not.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto rosenbrock = [](const Series &x) {
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    return (b - a * a).square() * 100.0 + (1.0 - a).square();
  };

  for (const auto family : {dfo::PSBasisFamily::Canonical, dfo::PSBasisFamily::RandomOrtho}) {
    dfo::PSConfig config;
    config.basis_family = family;
    config.search_strategy = dfo::PSSearchStrategy::Off;
    const dfo::PSOutcome o = dfo::pattern_search_minimizer(rosenbrock, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}), config);
    out.writeln(static_cast<int>(family), ": evaluations =", o.diagnostics.evaluations, ", cache hits =", o.diagnostics.cache_hits);
  }
}
```

### Example 3

Refreshing the random basis less often.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace dfo = pluss::subsp::math::optimization;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto rosenbrock = [](const Series &x) {
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    return (b - a * a).square() * 100.0 + (1.0 - a).square();
  };

  for (const std::int64_t interval : {1, 10}) {
    dfo::PSConfig config;
    config.basis_refresh_interval = interval;
    out.writeln("refresh every", interval, ": evaluations =", dfo::pattern_search_minimizer(rosenbrock, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}), config).diagnostics.evaluations);
  }
}
```

